From 3fa1a43c4f24e97c438cfafa66612700c0bf339f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:07:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: omap_hsmmc: restore the context on system resume

A host whose SDIO card is kept powered across system suspend stays
runtime active, so omap_hsmmc_runtime_resume() and its
omap_hsmmc_context_restore() don't run on resume. The module is idled by
ti-sysc in the noirq phase anyway, and on OMAP4 its power domain (L4PER)
can lose logic in suspend to RAM. After resume the controller then runs
with reset registers and the first SDIO command never completes: on a
Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 10.1 (BCM4330 on mmc5 with keep-power-in-suspend)
resume hangs in brcmfmac's resume callback until the watchdog resets
the board.

Restore the context in the system resume callback as well;
omap_hsmmc_context_restore() only acts when the registers differ from
the saved ones.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c
index de5a3b70107d..183c37025908 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c
@@ -2023,6 +2023,13 @@ static int omap_hsmmc_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(host->dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * A host that stayed runtime active across suspend (e.g. for an SDIO
+	 * card kept powered) didn't go through runtime resume, but its module
+	 * may have been idled by the bus driver and lost its context.
+	 */
+	omap_hsmmc_context_restore(host);
+
 	clk_prepare_enable(host->dbclk);
 
 	if (!(host->mmc->pm_flags & MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER))
-- 
2.55.0

